// Package-facing view of the canonical remote execution transport.
// Jetpack owns no second wire protocol, CAS, or scheduler. The canonical build
// engine owns host bindings, capabilities, deterministic builder selection,
// grants, and signed result statements. Its HMAC-SHA256 envelope covers actions,
// outputs, logs, worker proof, and execution identity before accepting results.
